 "previous_release": "commit 5560b5e (main of 9 November; on CUDA the arithmetic of the 8 November release b959c89), run beside this release on the same drives the same day, its drafter runs with its own sidecar",
 "changes": "scheduling, caching and block width only, no arithmetic change: one reader thread woken per queued read chunk, after the pool lock is released (DS4_K3_WAKE); an expert evicted from VRAM is copied down to the host pool only if it was used more often lately than the entry it would displace (DS4_K3_COPYDOWN_ADMIT); the shared expert runs while the routed experts' reads are in flight, and the next layer's router runs with this layer's (DS4_K3_CUDA_OVERLAP, DS4_K3_CUDA_LOOKAHEAD); decode prefetch of 2 of the 3 most likely next-layer experts into VRAM and up to 4 more of the top 8 into the host pool (DS4_K3_PREFETCH_HOST); prefetch hints in verification blocks (DS4_K3_VERIFY_HINTS); verification blocks of up to 32 rows with the adaptive gate on by default (DS4_K3_QWEN_ROWS, DS4_K3_QWEN_ADAPT)",
 "drafter": "Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B-Base, revision da87bfb608c14b7cf20ba1ce41287e8de496c0cd, float16 on the same GPU; proposals of 2 to 31 tokens make blocks of up to 32 rows; on raw text the gate starts at 0.6 and adapts within 0.6 to 0.95",
 "hardware": "one RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell (96 GB) in a 70 GiB VM; RAID0 of three NVMe with 79,365 experts; second NVMe with 11,768 (the other 3,067 plus 8,701 copies); the Thunderbolt NVMe of the 6 to 8 November runs was not attached",
 "settings": "documented defaults, DS4_K3_TRACE_HASH=1, -c 2048 for the standard rows, greedy, one fresh process per run; long-context rows with DS4_K3_DSA=<indexer file>, DS4_K3_CACHE_CAP and -c equal to the context; raw mode except the chat rows, which use the chat template with DS4_K3_QWEN_CHAT=1 DS4_K3_QWEN_CONF=0.9 DS4_K3_QWEN_ADAPT=0.6,0.95,0.02,0.1",
